ablit-runtime.patch: run-time abliteration for LakyFx TensorFold TP3 (runtime snapshot 61357deb, extracted by its
extract.py into $DATA_DIR/build/source). Apache-2.0, like the TensorFold sources it changes. Changes, in short:
  - zig/src/families/dsv41/abl.zig (new): TF_ABLIT loads a rank-1 direction per layer; after attn.wo_b each rank
    applies y -= lambda * mask[row] * (r . y) r to its fp32 partial (linear, so the all-gathered sum gets the same edit).
  - cublas.zig: Sdgmm and a k=1 Sgemm. model.zig / prompt.zig / round.zig: the edit and the per-row mask.
  - lanes.zig: each slot carries its stream steer (one byte in the fill_begin frame to the followers).
  - core lanes/engine_api/lane_host, server chat/openai/serve: steer from the model id (-ablit / -stock) or a boolean
    "ablit" field; TF_ABLIT_DEFAULT for the plain id; an edited request gets its own prompt-cache namespace.
  - core lane_host/lanes stream, dsv41 lanes.zig: TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD=1 runs a decode round of the live streams
    between a prompt's chunks, so a long prompt no longer stops everyone else's decode. Ported from Mia's AI Lab
    patch 0023 (Track D) of MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-4x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold (Apache-2.0).
  - core lane_host/lanes engine+backend, native cuda, dsv41 lanes.zig: with TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD=1 a prompt is read one
    chunk per host turn (prefillStep), rotating between admitted prompts, so a request that arrives during a long
    prompt starts at once. Ported from Mia's AI Lab patches 0031 (Mauvis Ledford) and 0032, same repository.
git apply skips these lines.

